keting  director of shopping center we had an  exhibition area where we wanted to do  something for children and then we got  the idea of making the gingerbread city  since then bergen's gingerbread town has  morphed into a major tourist attraction  some 100,000 visitors flocked to see it  each year  some of them even join in to help build  the town there are five hours together  and building all these houses and all  these features who is in a musical for  children and family it's called the  Christmas the magic of Christmas  we made a free bomb it's the little  train that goes up and down the hills in  Bergen picking up the kids build a  different themed house each year this  year's theme was Halloween the  architecture of the miniature town is  certainly diverse the train chugging  along a tiny track leads from buildings  in the Norwegian style to the Eiffel  Tower and maybe a short stop at London's  iconic Big Ben berrigan's delectable  gingerbread city will be on display  throughout the Christmas season until  December 31st
 

